cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this analysis or its figures, please cite it as below."
title: "Observed AI Exposure Across the Wage Distribution"
authors:
  - family-names: Daly
    given-names: Brendan
type: software
# Working correction; set date-released when publishing the corrected release.
version: "1.1.0-dev"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/brdaly/ai-wages"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible descriptive analysis joining Anthropic's March 2026 hybrid
  observed-exposure measure to a legacy O*NET wage scrape, with an older
  predicted-automatability score as a separate comparison. The corrected
  672-occupation sample has a modest positive wage-exposure association.
  Frozen inputs and coverage limits are documented; this is not an estimate
  of wage or employment effects.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - labor economics
  - wages
  - AI adoption
  - Anthropic Economic Index
